{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZsf2zwFcbvFMKyBifbd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I've found all the necessary components. Let me now move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class. Add OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Fetches the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException(404)\n   - Checks if any shipment for this order has status CONFIRMED\n   - If CONFIRMED exists, throws ConflictException(409) without changing anything\n   - Otherwise, transitions order to CANCELLED, updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, saves, and returns the order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Before creating a shipment, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(409).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - for operations (like shipment creation) blocked because order is cancelled\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` - for cancel attempts blocked by confirmed shipments\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an active order successfully\n   - Cancelling succeeds when called again (idempotency)\n   - Cancellation blocked by CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Unknown order returns 404\n   - Verify CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test for:\n   - Rejecting shipment creation for a cancelled order with 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:** Initially considered using a single error code for both scenarios (ORDER_CANCELLED), but the ticket distinguishes between \"shipment creation on cancelled order\" (409) and \"cancel blocked by confirmed shipment\" (409). These are different error conditions, so separate codes makes sense for client debugging.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path - Cancel active order with CREATED shipments:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller fetches order from repository\n3. Controller queries all shipments by orderId\n4. For each shipment: verify status is not CONFIRMED (if any is, throw ConflictException and stop)\n5. If all clear: update order.status to CANCELLED\n6. Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n7. Save updated order and shipments\n8. Return updated order (200 OK)\n\n*Error path - Already cancelled:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (order already CANCELLED)\n2. Controller fetches order\n3. No shipments are CONFIRMED (because order is already cancelled)\n4. Update order to CANCELLED (no-op)\n5. No shipments to update\n6. Return updated order (200 OK) - idempotent success\n\n*Error path - Has confirmed shipment:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Controller fetches order\n3. Finds shipment with status CONFIRMED\n4. Throws ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT code (409)\n5. Nothing persists - transaction rolls back\n\n*Error path - Unknown order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (orderId not found)\n2. Controller's findById returns null\n3. Throws ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND (404)\n\n*Shipment creation on cancelled order:*\n1. POST /shipments (order status is CANCELLED)\n2. ShipmentController checks order status before creating\n3. Order not found - keeps current behaviour (creates shipment)\n4. Order is CANCELLED - throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED (409)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest new tests:\n- `cancels_active_order_with_created_shipments` - verify order status changes, shipments cancelled, returns order\n- `cancelling_cancelled_order_succeeds` - verify second cancel succeeds with no changes\n- `cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment` - setup order with CONFIRMED shipment, verify 409 returned and nothing changes\n- `cancel_unknown_order_returns_404` - verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\nShipmentControllerTest new test:\n- `creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order_rejected_with_409` - create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\nNow I'll implement these changes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":20946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ba114ee-a78c-4c4d-b9e1-bc9febdbd24f","uuid":"626e1a8e-28ce-4696-bd5e-144ed3bfc2be","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:39:00.785Z","request_id":"req_011CfZsf2dben1ruQg2fmgz8"}
