ges** - Only modified:\n   - Order.kt (added status field)\n   - OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added order cancellation check)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId)\n   - ApiError.kt (added error codes)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt** - Added `status: OrderStatus` field with default ACTIVE value. Added OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED. Change is necessary.\n- **OrderController.kt** - Added cancel endpoint, injected shipmentRepository. Endpoint implements the full cancellation logic with atomic transaction semantics (all-or-nothing). Change is necessary.\n- **ShipmentController.kt** - Added orderRepository injection and check to prevent creating shipments for CANCELLED orders. Change is necessary.\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order. Change is necessary.\n- **ApiError.kt** - Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes. Change is necessary.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 tests covering: successful cancellation with shipment updates, idempotent retry, blocked by confirmed shipment, and unknown order. Tests are necessary.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 test covering: rejection of shipment creation for cancelled order. Test is necessary.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Customers may cancel an order until a carrier has accepted a shipment for it. Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with atomic all-or-nothing semantics, status tracking, idempotent retry support, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with atomic transaction logic\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to prevent shipment creation on CANCELLED orders\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added