cellation logic with atomic transaction semantics (all-or-nothing). Change is necessary.\n- **ShipmentController.kt** - Added orderRepository injection and check to prevent creating shipments for CANCELLED orders. Change is necessary.\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order. Change is necessary.\n- **ApiError.kt** - Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes. Change is necessary.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 tests covering: successful cancellation with shipment updates, idempotent retry, blocked by confirmed shipment, and unknown order. Tests are necessary.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 test covering: rejection of shipment creation for cancelled order. Test is necessary.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Customers may cancel an order until a carrier has accepted a shipment for it. Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with atomic all-or-nothing semantics, status tracking, idempotent retry support, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with atomic transaction logic\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to prevent shipment creation on CANCELLED orders\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 4 tests for cancel endpoint scenarios\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for blocked shipment creation\n\nTests:\n- `cancels_active_order_and_cancels_created_shipments`: Verifies successful cancellation updates order status and cancels CREATED shipments\n- `cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_succeeds`: Verifies idempotent retry behavior\n- `cancellation_is_blocked_by_a_confirmed_shipment`: Verifies 409 rejection with no state changes when CONFIRMED shipment exists\n- `cancelling_a_non_existent_order_returns_404`: Verifies 404 for unknown orders\n- `rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order_with_error_envelope`: Verifies 409 rejection when creating shipment for CANCELLED order\n\nVerification: Ran `./mvnw clean test` from sample-service/ - BUILD SUCCESS with 18 tests passing (4 new order tests + 1 new shipment test + all existing tests)\n\nNot done: None - all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no unrelated files modified.","ttft_ms":4940,"type":"result","duration_ms":153451,"uuid":"ee96c17a-37bc-4d61-8c6c-6c382bb8dd0f","ttft_stream_ms":627,"time_to_request_ms":24,"first_content_frame_ms":628,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

